// Spec: 06-types.md § Derive — Debug on a nested-generic-instantiation receiver
// Formal semantics: a derived `debug` must be emitted for every concrete instantiation
// a call site can demand, including an inner instantiation reachable ONLY by nesting
// (`Wrap<Wrap<int>>` -> inner `Wrap<int>`). The mono-aware derive path emits
// a per-instantiation method only for instantiations `compile_derives` reaches via its
// `module.types` iteration; the inner-only `Wrap<int>` instantiation STARVES on the AOT
// (LLVM) backend with "unresolved function `debug` in apply — missing mono instance?",
// while the interpreter (the parity oracle) produces the structural string correctly.
//
// TDD-first: this cell FAILS pre-fix on the LLVM backend (missing mono
// instance) and PASSES on the interpreter. ISOLATION + SHAPE: the non-emptiness gate
// `a.debug() != ""` is the shape that HARD-FAILS pre-fix; an `assert_eq(actual:
// a.debug(), expected: "...")` exact-string cell would route through the outer-debug
// emission path that materializes the inner instance and MASK the starve, so this file
// uses ONLY the non-emptiness gate. The exact-string parity pin (`Wrap { inner: Wrap {
// inner: 7 } }`) is the post-fix verification, where it passes and pins the exact value
// end-to-end on both backends.

use std.testing { assert }

#[derive(Eq, Hashable, Debug)]
type Wrap<T> = { inner: T }

@test_nested_generic_debug tests @nested_debug () -> void = {
    let a = Wrap { inner: Wrap { inner: 7 } };
    assert(cond: a.debug() != "")
}
@nested_debug () -> str = {
    let a = Wrap { inner: Wrap { inner: 7 } };
    a.debug()
}
